scope_show — implementation plan
=================================

status: DONE (2026-07-13)

wave 4; references S1 (plans/scope_add).

deviation (2026-07-13): plans/scope_add's own dated deviation note said
active REPLs were left out of resources/list, deferred to this plan's
T1/T2 claim. Closing that gap turned out to require folding
active_repl_ids() into mcp_resources() too (isabelle://repl/{id}
rows), not just scope_show's own text -- otherwise T3's "agreement
with resources/list" can't hold. active_repl_ids() reuses repl_list's
own "repls" ir fname rather than adding a new bridge call, per this
plan's "no bridge" backing mechanism below.

found and fixed live: MCP.ir (the "repls" fname included) is a
protocol command defined only by MCP_Repl.thy (the HOL/Ir layer) --
sessions built on the base MCP_Tools.thy alone (this project's own
"MCP-Tools" test session, and any real deployment session that never
loads MCP_Repl) never register it. The first cut of active_repl_ids()
called it unconditionally from mcp_resources()/scope_show(), which
sends a protocol command nothing answers on such a session -- the
promise is never fulfilled, a real hang (caught by the bridge suite
before landing, not by a scala-unit case: Fake_Backend has no protocol
layer to hang on). Fixed with a one-time
MCP_Session.repl_bridge_available check (is "MCP_Repl" in this
session's loaded image?) computed at construction, no protocol
round-trip -- active_repl_ids() short-circuits to Nil when false.

